      "text": "The script finds the first monthly table, takes the four needed columns (SMALL LoPRIOR, BIG LoPRIOR, SMALL HiPRIOR, BIG HiPRIOR), and computes 0.5*(Small Lo + Big Lo) - 0.5*(Small Hi + Big Hi). Missing-value codes (-99.99, -999) become NaN and months with missing inputs are dropped.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nFN = \"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_1_0.csv\"\nOUT = \"output.csv\"\n\n\ndef is_missing(x):\n    return x is None or np.isnan(x) or np.isclose(x, -99.99) or np.isclose(x, -999.0)\n\n\ndef to_float(s):\n    try:\n        v = float(s)\n    except (ValueError, TypeError):\n        return np.nan\n    return np.nan if is_missing(v) else v\n\n\ndef norm(s):\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", s.strip().upper())\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(FN, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    # locate the title of the first (value-weighted monthly) block\n    start = -1\n    for i, l in enumerate(lines):\n        low = l.lower()\n        if \"value weighted\" in low and \"monthly\" in low:\n            start = i\n            break\n    if start < 0:\n        start = -1  # fallback: first monthly-looking block in file\n\n    header = None\n    started = False\n    rows = []\n    for l in lines[start + 1:]:\n        s = l.strip()\n        if not s:\n            if started:\n                break\n            continue\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in s.split(\",\")]\n        if not started and parts[0] == \"\" and header is None:\n            header = parts\n            continue\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{6}\", parts[0]):\n            started = True\n            rows.append(parts)\n        else:\n            if started:\n                break  # end of monthly table\n\n    if header is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Header not found\")\n\n    hnames = [norm(h) for h in header]\n\n    def col_idx(name, fallback):\n        n = norm(name)\n        if n in hnames:\n            return hnames.index(n)\n        return fallback\n\n    i_sl = col_idx(\"SMALL LoPRIOR\", 1)\n    i_bl = col_idx(\"BIG LoPRIOR\", 4)\n    i_sh = col_idx(\"SMALL HiPRIOR\", 3)\n    i_bh = col_idx(\"BIG HiPRIOR\", 6)\n\n    out_dates = []\n    out_vals = []\n    for parts in rows:\n        def get(idx):\n            return to_float(parts[idx]) if idx < len(parts) else np.nan\n\n        sl, bl, sh, bh = get(i_sl), get(i_bl), get(i_sh), get(i_bh)\n        if any(np.isnan(v) for v in (sl, bl, sh, bh)):\n            continue\n        val = 0.5 * (sl + bl) - 0.5 * (sh + bh)\n        out_dates.append(int(parts[0]))\n        out_vals.append(val)\n\n    df = pd.DataFrame({\"date\": out_dates, \"value\": out_vals})\n    df[\"date\"] = df[\"date\"].astype(int)\n    df.to_csv(OUT, index=False)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
